  "narrative": "The new stratum analyses confirm that the accepted outcome_006 feature_021 association is broad across major binary strata in this supplied dataset. H47 within feature_002=1, H55 within feature_034=1, and H56 within feature_060=1 have very large signed estimates in the weaker-dependency direction: +0.8144, +0.7976, and +0.7999, respectively, with 95% intervals far above the approximate clinical threshold for outcome_006 (~0.0093) and with adequate cell counts. I therefore accept these as dataset associations, consistent with H38 and H40, and close them because the central feature_021/outcome_006 pattern has been characterized across the key strata. They remain associations within this dataset only, not causal effects or generalizable claims; the strata are overlapping and correlated, so these are not independent replications, but their magnitude makes multiplicity and chance unlikely explanations for the main pattern. H57 and H58 test whether the association is stronger in the feature_034=1 or age>=55 subgroups. Both have negative signed interaction point estimates and intervals that include zero, threshold-crossing positive values, and threshold-crossing opposite-direction values; there is no clinically meaningful evidence of stronger effect modification, so I leave them unresolved as low-priority and close them. The age interaction also depends on a predictor with substantial missingness, so it could reflect selection under missingness as well as real heterogeneity. H59 tests feature_021 on outcome_003. The signed estimate is tiny (+0.0015) and its upper bound (+0.0212) is below the approximate outcome_003 threshold (~0.025), so the evidence does not support a clinically meaningful positive feature_021 association for outcome_003; I reject that specific positive clinical claim. Alternative outcome_006 predictor screens were generally uninformative or borderline: feature_027 is below threshold with wide uncertainty, feature_055 level comparison is opposite to the claimed direction, feature_037 is borderline but imprecise, feature_054 is weak, and feature_063 is opposite to the claimed direction. The one specificity screen worth further checking is H61, feature_050 on outcome_006, because it has prevalence similar to feature_021, a point estimate well above threshold (+0.0262), and a wide interval that includes both clinically meaningful positive and opposite effects. I request independent validation for H61 because it is the most informative non-central borderline association: if it validates, feature_050 may represent a related predictor axis or potential confounder; if it is null, it strengthens the distinctiveness of feature_021 for outcome_006 in this dataset. No other validation request is made because the accepted feature_021 pattern is already unusually large and internally consistent across strata.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after iteration 4 appraise. Accepted outcome_006 feature_021 dataset associations (less-negative dependency, direction +): H38 overall +0.8019 [0.7823,0.8216]; H40 feature_002=0 +0.7897 [0.7611,0.8183]; H47 feature_002=1 +0.8144 [0.7873,0.8416]; H55 feature_034=1 +0.7976 [0.7723,0.8229]; H56 feature_060=1 +0.7999 [0.7724,0.8274]. All intervals are far above the approximate outcome_006 threshold ~0.0093; these are associations in the supplied data only, not causal or generalizable. Interactions H57 feature_034 and H58 age>=55 are opposite in sign, imprecise, and closed unresolved; age missingness limits H58. H59 outcome_003 feature_021 rejected for positive clinical effect because upper 0.0212 is below threshold ~0.025. Other outcome_006 predictor screens closed unresolved: H27 feature_037 borderline imprecise, H31 feature_054 weak, H33 feature_063 signed negative, H60 feature_027 weak, H62 feature_055 level_001 vs level_003 negative. H61 feature_050 is active and pending independent validation because point estimate +0.0262 exceeds threshold but interval [-0.0146,0.0671] is too wide. Decision: if H61 validates, investigate conditional/joint feature_021 vs feature_050 structure and confounding; if null, close as alternative marker screen and keep feature_021/outcome_006 as the central dataset finding. Continue avoiding low-prior broad feature_021 outcome panels unless outcome specificity is directly at issue. Threshold reminders: outcome_006/014 ~0.0093, outcome_005/012/015/003 ~0.025; estimates are already signed to hypothesis direction.",
